🟢 EASIEST WAY (Still Using Railway)

Railway can deploy directly from your local machine without GitHub.

Step 1 — Install Railway CLI

Download Node if you don’t have it, then install:

npm install -g @railway/cli
Step 2 — Login
railway login

It’ll open a browser. Click approve. Done.

Step 3 — Inside Your Project Folder

Open terminal in VS Code (inside your project folder):

railway init

Choose:

Create new project

Step 4 — Deploy
railway up

It uploads your project directly.

No GitHub needed.

Step 5 — Generate Domain

In Railway dashboard:

Go to your project

Networking

Generate domain

Boom. Live backend.
